## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/filterfrequencies.html
- Summary (EN): Filter Frequencies strengthens, weakens, or removes fine or broad detail in an image at a chosen spatial scale. It works by converting the image into frequency space, applying a mask, and converting it back.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Filter Frequencies renforce, atténue ou supprime les détails fins ou larges d'une image à une échelle spatiale choisie.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: image to filter", "filter (optional): image used directly as the frequency-domain mask; when connected, the Frequency and Anisotropy controls are disabled"]

- Key parameters: ["Scale: multiplies the filtered result; above 1 boosts the kept band, below 1 attenuates it", "Frequency: center of the kept band, from 0 (lowest, broad content) to 1 (finest detail)", "Width (under Frequency): full width of the kept band around Frequency", "Smooth (under Frequency): softens the band edges instead of using a hard cutoff", "Angle (under Anisotropy): center direction of an angular wedge, from 0 to 360 degrees", "Width (under Anisotropy): angular extent of the wedge; default 360 keeps all directions", "Smooth (under Anisotropy): softens the angular edges of the wedge", "Reflect: mirrors the wedge to the opposite direction (Angle plus 180)"]

- Caveats: ["A hard cutoff in frequency space can cause ringing artifacts; smoothing the band usually gives a cleaner image", "The Frequency and Anisotropy controls are disabled whenever the filter input is wired", "The page describes the node as available since Houdini 22.0"]

